An NFA over Σ = {0, 1} has states {A, B, C, D}, start state A, final state {D} and the transitions below (∅ means no move). The minimal DFA equivalent to this NFA has how many states? <span style="display:block;font-family:Consolas,'DejaVu Sans Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre;margin:8px 0">|    0    |    1
------+---------+--------
  A   |  {A}    | {A, B}
  B   |  {C}    |  {C}
  C   |  {D}    |  {D}
  D   |    ∅    |    ∅</span>

An NFA has states {A, B, C}, start state A, final state {C} and the transitions below. Counting only reachable subset states, how many states does the DFA produced by the subset construction have? <span style="display:block;font-family:Consolas,'DejaVu Sans Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre;margin:8px 0">|    0    |   1
------+---------+------
  A   | {A, B}  | {A}
  B   |    ∅    | {C}
  C   |  {C}    | {C}</span>
